# NestedText v3 - THE CROSS-CORPUS INDEX
# Written 2026-09-13 as step one of 10.0.0, ordered by intake-one answer 49.
# This is the file DOMAIN-TYPE-DEFINITION reads: not a list of corpora, but a list
# of MECHANISMS, each naming the corpora that use it and what the release takes.
# Read in reverse: the release-bindings come last and are the most actionable.

sources:
    corpora: 27 folders plus 10 loose files under cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples
    measured-files: 768 dtd, mod and ent
    study-files: 69 nt under full-study, 5 source documents fully transmigrated
    detail-passes-done: tei dita-shells office-dtds-daisy mathml-docbook-xhtml11 svg xhtml11 docbook daisy jats-duo xhtml-duo ooxml tocjs dita11 lwdita xdita ditaversion mathml office dtds dtbook docbook-sch svg-modules tei-modules dita-specializations

mechanisms:

    empty-hook-invoked-at-once:
        strength: STRONGEST cross-corpus pattern found; five corpora, one idiom
        corpora:
            tei: TEI.extensions.ent declared empty, invoked on the next line
            svg: 49 .attrib collections and both redecl placeholders declared empty
            xmlschema: percent-p and percent-s redefinable in the consumer internal subset
            jats: the customization quartet, classes mixes models modules, one set per profile
            dita: every domain ships a .mod and .ent pair, the .ent declared ahead
        shape:
            > Declare the extension point EMPTY. Invoke it immediately. A consumer that
            > wants nothing pays nothing; a consumer that wants something declares it
            > BEFORE the include and the first declaration binds.
        release-binding: LAW.ASK.11 is this idiom already; stream 4 and stream 14 both depend on it holding

    precedence-by-named-slot:
        corpora:
            svg: prefw and postfw, TWO override points, before and after the framework, marked-section IGNORE by default
            xmlschema: the consumer internal subset as the single named override site
            dita: catalog.xml resolves identity to location, so a path is never hard-coded
        shape:
            > Precedence is a declared POSITION, not a race. First-wins is what happens
            > when nobody declared where an override belongs.
        release-binding:
            > Stream 4, depth as precedence: depth.dtd declares WHERE an override may
            > sit, the reverse read resolves which fired. This is the F14 fix in law.

    one-source-many-emissions:
        corpora:
            tei: ODD emits dtd, rng and rnc together; a quartet per module
            svg: svg11-tiny 197 lines modular AND svg11-tiny-flat 2808 lines, same profile, factor 14
            docbook: 5.0 ships dtd rng sch xsd nvdl at once
            dita: 188 files at v1_2 becoming 656 at v1_3, generated and catalogued
            lwdita: conductor.xml imports build-html and build-markdown, two outputs one source
        shape:
            > The fan-out is never hand-kept. One literate source, many emissions, a
            > catalog to resolve them.
        release-binding:
            > Stream 17: 143 commands to 429 files is this curve. It is survivable
            > ONLY as generation. DITA at 656 hand-kept files would have collapsed.

    parallel-tracks-aligned:
        corpora:
            daisy: four tracks, dtbook 82 elements text, dtbsmil 14 timing, ncx 18 navigation, oebpkg package
            tei: att.global.linking, corresp synch sameAs copyOf next prev exclude select
            tei: att.fragmentable part Y N I M F, and att.divLike sample initial medial final unknown complete
        shape:
            > A work too large to read linearly declares its own navigation and its own
            > alignment. No single track is the work; the work is the tracks, aligned.
        release-binding:
            > Stream 15, the TEI cache subset. ncx is the reverse read: arrive anywhere,
            > know the position. A 384-question intake is a work too long to read linearly.
            > DAISY caution measured: oeb12.ent is 48964 bytes and exactly ONE file
            > includes it, so the tracks-share-entities claim is narrow, not broad.

    profiles-as-additive-deltas:
        corpora:
            xhtml: strict 966 lines, transitional 1189, heads byte-identical through line 60, delta plus 12 presentational elements
            svg: full, basic, tiny from one module set
            jats: articleauthoring versus journalpublishing, subsetting as profiling
            dita: technicalContent SPECIALIZES base, never edits it
        shape:
            > One skeleton, additive profiles. A profile constrains or extends; it never
            > forks the base.
        release-binding:
            > gate-1 linux, gate-2 windows, gate-3 macos is this exactly.
            > Stream 18, per-command laws abolished: a command SPECIALIZES a subset's
            > law by constraining it, the way technicalContent specializes topic.

    the-ceiling-of-a-dtd:
        corpora:
            docbook: 4.2 to 4.5 dtd only, 5.0 every grammar, 5.1 NO dtd at all
            docbook: rng for datatypes, sch for co-occurrence, nvdl to dispatch
        shape:
            > A DTD cannot express co-occurrence constraints, context-dependent content,
            > or datatypes on text. Past that line the answer is a second instrument.
        release-binding:
            > The suite already has the second instrument and calls it checker/. Stream
            > 19 converges the corpus into every subset; this mechanism says where the
            > convergence STOPS. Name that line in the release rather than meet it at 11.0.0.

    trust-classes-as-syntax:
        corpora:
            dtd-variants: PCDATA parsed and escaped, CDATA raw except the close delimiter, NDATA never read by the processor
            dtd-variants: the four-format map, literal expanded binary escape across shell, dtd, yaml and nt
            arguments: quoted dollar-at dispatch only, eval banned, sanitize before interpolate
        shape:
            > The trust class is the syntax. NDATA means the processor records a URI and
            > a type and never opens the file; the APPLICATION resolves it.
        release-binding:
            > Stream 16, GLOSSARY.dtd: the alarm prefix carries the entity class.
            > percent-bang binds, at-bang is carried whole, dollar-bang is the bus.
            > The trust boundary becomes visible in prose rather than only in a DOCTYPE.

    registry-with-declared-escape:
        corpora:
            dita: every enumeration carries -dita-use-conref-target as its escape value
            jats: four override slots named ahead, never ad hoc
            xhtml-lat1: 254 flat rows, mnemonic to numeric to Unicode name to ISO set
        shape:
            > Name the values. Name the escape. Never leave the open case undeclared.
        release-binding:
            > Stream 11, MX.targets: named values plus a declared escape, because ecc
            > means every other variant. Stream 13, the eight-token ask registry.

    license-and-identity-travel-with-the-grammar:
        corpora:
            edoc: full SPDX dual-license header INSIDE the dtd
            jats: MODULE VERSION DATE PUBLIC SYSTEM PURPOSE SPONSOR header block
            tei: generated-from stamp, ODD 3.5.0 revision 3c0c64ec4, dated 2019-01-29
        shape:
            > A grammar states its own provenance, its own version and its own licence,
            > in band, so a copy found alone is still identifiable.
        release-binding:
            > Stream 14's version stamp is this. TEI stamps the revision it was generated
            > from; that is precisely what an inlined subset must carry.

    honest-underconstraint:
        corpora:
            xmlschema: the file states it is less restrictive than really intended, and that mutual exclusion is unenforced
            xmlschema: a DTD for XML Schemas that declares its own non-authority, prose being definitive
        shape:
            > Where the grammar cannot enforce, it SAYS SO in band rather than implying
            > enforcement it does not perform.
        release-binding:
            > The suite's partial verdict and the measured-reasoned-guessed confidence
            > ladder are the same discipline. A law that over-promises is a law that fails,
            > which is why LIVE became a rendering law and not an element.

what-is-not-yet-transmigrated:
    > Per-module content models for svg 49 modules, tei 20 modules, dita bookmap
    > learning machineryIndustry subjectScheme xnal, daisy dtbook 82 elements, docbook
    > 4.5 and the 5.1 schematron rule set: all transmigrated 2026-09-16
    > (svg-modules, tei-modules, dita-specializations, dtbook, docbook-sch).
    > None of these blocks a stream. Every stream's binding above is measured.
